## 🏗️ Architecture

### Two-Tier (Flask + MySQL in separate containers on a custom bridge network)

```text
                Host (AWS EC2)
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ┌─────────────────┐        ┌─────────────┐  │
│  │  flaskapp :5000 │───────►│ mysql :3306 │  │
│  └─────────────────┘        └─────────────┘  │
│            flask-net (user-defined bridge)   │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
        ▲
        │ :5000
     Browser
```

The Flask app reaches the database by container name (`mysql`) — Docker's internal DNS resolves it inside the user-defined network. No IPs hardcoded.

### Three-Tier MERN (Docker Compose)

```text
                Host (AWS EC2)
┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ┌──────────────┐   ┌──────────────┐   ┌───────────┐  │
│  │ frontend:3000│──►│ backend:5000 │──►│ mongo:27017│ │
│  │  (React)     │   │  (Node API)  │   │ (MongoDB)  │ │
│  └──────────────┘   └──────────────┘   └───────────┘  │
│              app-network (bridge)                      │
│                       mongo-data (named volume) ──────┘
└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
        ▲               ▲
        │ :3000         │ :5000 (API)
     Browser         curl / clients
```

