## 🔐 Secure Runtime (Class 46) — `docker run` Hardening

```bash
docker run -d \
  --name notes-app \
  --restart unless-stopped \
  --user 1000:1000 \
  --read-only \
  --tmpfs /tmp \
  --cap-drop=ALL \
  --security-opt no-new-privileges \
  --memory=512m \
  --cpus=1.0 \
  -p 8000:8000 \
  -v "$(pwd)/logs:/app/logs:rw" \
  --health-cmd="curl -f http://localhost:8000/health || exit 1" \
  --health-interval=30s \
  --health-retries=3 \
  --health-start-period=10s \
  django-notes-app:latest
```

| Flag | Why |
|------|-----|
| `--user 1000:1000` | Avoids root; reduces attack surface |
| `--read-only` | Immutable filesystem; writes go to explicit volumes/tmpfs only |
| `--cap-drop=ALL` | Removes all Linux capabilities |
| `--security-opt no-new-privileges` | Blocks privilege escalation (setuid) |
| `--memory` / `--cpus` | Resource limits; prevents abuse & noisy neighbors |
| `--restart unless-stopped` | Auto-restart on crash or host reboot |
| `--health-*` | Traffic only routes to healthy containers |

